<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eberhard II, Count of the Mark</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1255–1308</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eberhard II (c. 1255–1308) was Count of the Mark from 1277. He fought on the side of Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-duke-of-brabant">John I of Brabant</a> against the Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-worringen">Battle of Worringen</a> in 1288, whose outcome broke Cologne's dominance in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a> and secured his county's independence. He then expanded the Mark at the archbishopric's expense.</p></div>
